      // every row, and `edit url` on every row too, so a dynamically added endpoint and the Primary
      // row carry the same controls. The same two clicks on every row, so a registry entry cannot
      // vanish from one accidental press. What it takes away is different, so the hover says which
      // one: a registered entry leaves the registry; on the Primary row the SLOT is emptied, which is
      // the one thing this control was called `clear` here before. The verb behind each one is
      // recorded where it is sent (endpoint_clear {fn} in EndpointRow.clearPrimary, endpoint_remove
